  "summary": "A Roots blower moves air with two lobed rotors that turn in opposite directions without touching, kept in step by timing gears. Air is trapped between each rotor and the casing and carried from the inlet to the outlet; there is no internal compression — the pressure rises when the pocket opens to the higher-pressure discharge (backflow). Used for low pressure ratios such as aeration and pneumatic conveying.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Positive-displacement blower (rotary lobe)",
    "type": "Tri-lobe Roots blower, belt driven"
  },
